---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Contact' }];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Contact the editorial team for corrections, copyright complaints, or general questions."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  updated="16 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    We are a small editorial team. Email is the fastest way to reach us. Please use the
    correct address so your message reaches the right queue.
  </p>

  <h2>General and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
  </p>
  <p>Include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the page URL and the exact section,</li>
    <li>what is wrong and what it should say,</li>
    <li>a link or citation that supports the correction, and</li>
    <li>your name if you want credit for the correction.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Copyright and takedown</h2>
  <p>
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.grievanceEmail}`}>{SITE.grievanceEmail}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/takedown/">Copyright &amp; Takedown</a> page for the information we
    need and the timelines we follow. Do not send a public link to the disputed file.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cannot help with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Checking your result, registration, or admit card.</li>
    <li>Recovering a university portal password.</li>
    <li>Guaranteeing marks, ranks, scholarships, or admission.</li>
    <li>Sharing leaked papers or personal student data.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For official decisions, use the AKTU website or your institution's examination cell.
  </p>

  <h2>Response times</h2>
  <p>
    General messages are usually answered within a few working days. Copyright complaints
    are acknowledged within 24 hours and reviewed on the timeline described on the
    takedown page.
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">
    TODO: replace the placeholder email addresses and add a monitored phone number or
    postal address before launch if required by your jurisdiction.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
